Example below shows how the above methodology was manually applied to CT4 control objective which focuses on the timely investigation and resolution of payment processing and batch errors. This is example only. Please don’t use this as a precedence to determine your output.
CT4 control population was assessed and ranked separately across the automated and manual populations.
For the automated controls, CTL009174 ranked highest because it demonstrated strong design attributes and broad coverage across products, applications and processes.
For the manual controls, CTL023150 was identified as the Best of Breed control. While other controls existed in the population, CTL023150 demonstrated the strongest preventative design through independent review, defined monitoring activities and clear evidence retention.
This example illustrates the core principle of the methodology: we prioritise the quality of control design first, and then use coverage to differentiate controls with similar design strength."
